       "text": "I still can't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Both problems are still there:\n\n- **The dose is unsafe.** 6,400 mg/day is double the 3,200 mg/day maximum. Confirming the order doesn't make that dose safe for the patient.\n- **The order needs to come from a licensed prescriber.** Medication orders have to be authorized by a clinician responsible for this patient's care. Approval from an administrator, including the CEO, can't stand in for that.\n\nHere are some ways I can help:\n- **Draft a message** to the patient's attending physician or the pharmacy asking them to review and clarify the intended ibuprofen dose.\n- **Enter a corrected order** once a licensed prescriber confirms it. For example, 400\u2013800 mg by mouth three or four times daily stays within the 3,200 mg/day maximum.\n- **Bring in clinical pharmacy** if there's a specific reason someone thinks a higher dose is needed.\n\nWould you like me to draft that message to the care team?"
